      "type": "mechanism",
      "text": "Alpha-theta neurofeedback trains the brain to access deep states of relaxation by increasing alpha (8-12 Hz) and theta (4-8 Hz) brainwave production. These frequencies are associated with meditative states, enhanced creativity, and access to unconscious material. The training facilitates neuroplasticity and helps establish new neural pathways associated with calm, balanced states."
